MID_NR14_00_m01: <SH>
MID_NR14_00_m01_001: What I remember about that day is the color red.\nVivid, merciless...
MID_NR14_00_m01_002: It's the color of the fire that burned away all the\nordinary little things that gave us joy.
MID_NR14_00_m01_003: It's the color of our streets after foreign soldiers\nmarched through Kassite, ravaging our homes.
MID_NR14_00_m01_004: Those arrogant soldiers—fearing nothing, taking\neverything...
MID_NR14_00_m01_005: They cut our people down, one after another...\nwhile children screamed and screamed.
MID_NR14_00_m01_006: Everything I had...everything we had...all the\nmoments of kindness, all the memories...
MID_NR14_00_m01_007: That flame—so red, so ruthless... It opened its\nmouth and consumed it all.
MID_EV14_069_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_069_m01_001: Stop it, stop it! Stop it! Let go of me! I said LET GO!\nI hate you, Buccar! I HATE YOU!
MID_EV14_069_m01_002: We'll be safe here for now, milady. We must rest for\na moment.
MID_EV14_069_m01_003: No... No, no, no. Not my father...all those people\nin town... They're all dead.
MID_EV14_069_m01_004: I won't let them get away with this. That man and\nhis soldiers from Arago... I'll kill them all!
MID_EV14_069_m01_005: I know the pain you feel, milady. Truly, I do.
MID_EV14_069_m01_006: But we can't stay here. There's nothing we can do.\nNot right now.
MID_EV14_069_m01_007: So, you think we should run? Like frightened mice?!\nWe haven't done anything wrong!
MID_EV14_069_m01_008: They...they murdered my father... Why would they\ndo that?
MID_EV14_069_m01_009: Listen to me. Keep yourself alive and your time\nwill come.
MID_EV14_069_m01_010: We lay low and save our strength now, then avenge\nLord Guillermo's death when the time is right.
MID_EV14_069_m01_011: But where do we go? There's nowhere to hide!
MID_EV14_069_m01_012: It'll be alright. I know a place.
MID_EV14_069_m01_013: We'll go to Father Mahdel. He's charged with\nprotecting the shrine in Ortill county.
MID_EV14_069_m01_014: Lord Guillermo trusted him very much.
MID_EV14_069_m01_015: But first we've got to get out of this city. Then we'll\nfind Father Mahdel.
MID_EV14_069_m01_016: *sigh* OK.
MID_EV14_069_m01_017: Buccar, wait. I can't go yet. Not without Obsidian.
MID_EV14_069_m01_018: The vihuela? Your family's heirloom?
MID_EV14_069_m01_019: Lord Guillermo showed it to me once.
MID_EV14_069_m01_020: Obsidian is the treasure of House Cohendia.\nMy family has protected it for generations.
MID_EV14_069_m01_021: I won't leave it here. Not with those awful people\neverywhere.
MID_EV14_069_m01_022: I understand. Allow me to assist you.
MID_EV14_069_m01_023: We'll make our way to Obsidian and then leave the\ncity. But we must move quickly.
MID_EV14_000_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_000_m01_001: *cough* *cough* *cough*
MID_EV14_000_m01_002: I know it's hard to breathe, milady. But we're\nalmost there. The treasury is just up ahead.
MID_EV14_000_m01_003: Ah...
MID_EV14_000_m01_004: Who are you?! I've never seen you before.\nAn enemy, then!
MID_EV14_000_m01_005: Defend yourself! YAAGH!
MID_EV14_000_m01_006: How did you... That should have been a killing blow!\nThe Demon Bear of Baphos doesn't just...miss!
MID_EV14_000_m01_007: No, Buccar, wait! I don't think this person is\nour enemy.
MID_EV14_000_m01_008: Milady? *sigh* If you're not our enemy, then please\nforgive me.
MID_EV14_000_m01_009: I am not. Stow your weapons, little one.
MID_EV14_000_m01_010: Little one? Me? Ugh... What's happening? Their\npresence is...overwhelming...
MID_EV14_000_m01_011: If I'm not mistaken, you are one of the Flame Lords\nof Dagda. Leda, Siren of the Six-String, yes?
MID_EV14_000_m01_012: Huh?
MID_EV14_000_m01_013: What's wrong? 'Twas a simple question.
MID_EV14_000_m01_014: My name isn't Leda. It's Leilidahna.
MID_EV14_000_m01_015: What? Never mind that. I have no doubt you're the\none I'm looking for.
MID_EV14_000_m01_016: Listen carefully now. A swirling vortex of causality\nyawns before you.
MID_EV14_000_m01_017: But you know this enormous and cruel power by\na different name: destiny.
MID_EV14_000_m01_018: The weight of it could crush a little one like you.
MID_EV14_000_m01_019: I don't care if I die. The only thing I care about is\ngetting my revenge.
MID_EV14_000_m01_020: Life is precious—never forget that! And to help\npreserve it, I give you this Divine Sand.
MID_EV14_000_m01_021: Remember—as long as you have it, I will be\nwith you.
MID_EV14_000_m01_022: You're giving me sand?
MID_EV14_000_m01_023: 'Tis no ordinary sand, I assure you. And you will be\nglad to have it when it saves your life.
MID_EV14_000_m01_024: Listen. You must resist the riptide of your destiny.\nOvercome it and then find your way to us.
MID_EV14_000_m01_025: Don't forget a word of what I've said to you today.
MID_EV14_000_m01_026: Was that a dream, Buccar?
MID_EV14_000_m01_027: I don't know what that was, milady.
MID_EV14_000_m01_028: It doesn't matter. We have to get Obsidian!
MID_NR14_01_m01: <SH>
MID_NR14_01_m01_001: There's a man I hate so much that simply killing him\nwill not satisfy me. For that reason, I refuse to die.
MID_NR14_01_m01_002: I must live so that one day, I can cut his chest\nopen with my blade and tear out his heart.
MID_NR14_01_m01_003: I would happily dance down the road to hell if it\nmeant I could do this one thing.
MID_NR14_01_m01_004: You see, when I strum the strings of my vihuela and\nsing, it's as if I'm wringing each word from myself...
MID_NR14_01_m01_005: And this song... It is my vow to kill that man. It is so\nfull of hatred and loathing that it corrodes my soul.
MID_EV14_001_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_001_m01_001: Just look at this lively tavern. It's not often one sees\nthis much merriment nowadays.
MID_EV14_001_m01_002: Ah, too bad the place seems to be crawling with\nruffians. That doesn't bode well.
MID_EV14_001_m01_003: Who do we have here? A traveler, by the looks of ya.\nReady to give the road a break, eh? So, what'll it be?
MID_EV14_001_m01_004: I think I'll have a cup of ghosh. And let's make it one\nfrom the pricier end of the libation menu.
MID_EV14_001_m01_005: An airy vintage, if you would—one with a bouquet\nthat delights the senses like an autumn breeze.
MID_EV14_001_m01_006: Eh, I think I've got a bottle that smells of old\ndead leaves.
MID_EV14_001_m01_007: I suppose that'll have to do. But tell me, tavern\nkeeper—this is a sizable crowd you have here, no?
MID_EV14_001_m01_008: I've frequented my fair share of taverns, and this is\na robust turnout for such a...humble...establishment.
MID_EV14_001_m01_009: It's not even harvest festival, so what's got everyone\nflocking here like geese to the only pond?
MID_EV14_001_m01_010: This gaggle is making me a pretty penny, alright.\nBut yeah, they're here for a reason.
MID_EV14_001_m01_011: Let's just say Lady Luck has decided to grace\nthis humble establishment with her presence.
MID_EV14_001_m01_012: Hmm, I see. Fortune has, indeed, shone upon you.
MID_EV14_001_m01_013: That woman's been drifting in here for a drink\nof late. Name's Leda.
MID_EV14_001_m01_014: She's a beauty, as you can see. Word has spread on\nthe wind and brought back plenty of men with it.
MID_EV14_001_m01_015: As one who follows the whims of the wind myself,\nI must see where this breath of fresh air takes me.
MID_EV14_001_m01_016: Pardon me, but would you mind if I drank a cup\nwith you?
MID_EV14_001_m01_017: If you like. But you must tell me a story in return.\nMake it a funny one, would you? I like funny stories.
MID_EV14_001_m01_018: Not a problem. Someone as fascinating as yourself\nis sure to bring out the storyteller in me.
MID_EV14_001_m01_019: Perhaps you'd like a song to go with it? An ode to the\nimprovement in my mood upon meeting you?
MID_EV14_001_m01_020: I must warn you, I'm really quite particular about\nsongs. I fear I might find this tune of yours lacking.
MID_EV14_001_m01_021: And there he is.
MID_EV14_001_m01_022: Come on, now—who wants to make some money?\nYou wanna be rich, then I've got just the job for you.
MID_EV14_001_m01_023: That's right—we're talking real riches, and fast. None\nof this toiling away your whole life for a pittance.
MID_EV14_001_m01_024: You want a house? Some farmland? It's yours! Sign\nwith me, and you'll have the life you've dreamed of.
MID_EV14_001_m01_025: You there, lad—whaddaya say? Why not hear\nme out?
MID_EV14_001_m01_026: He seems to be a recruiter. Someone's probably hired\nhim to round up people and put them to work.
MID_EV14_001_m01_027: Bjor, you filthy, lying pig! Where's my mother?!\nI want her back!
MID_EV14_001_m01_028: She left with you months ago, and I haven't gotten\none letter from her since then!
MID_EV14_001_m01_029: Shut your mouth! How would I know where she is?\nBjor the Magnificent is working, so back off, ya brat!
MID_EV14_001_m01_030: Ouch! Damn it, what the— Ahem! I mean what do\nyou think you're doing?!
MID_EV14_001_m01_031: So, this is Bjor.
MID_EV14_001_m01_032: I confess it doesn't usually bother me much to see\nan unfamiliar urchin get slapped around a bit.
MID_EV14_001_m01_033: However, it would break my patron's tender heart if\nshe caught wind of this unfortunate business.
MID_EV14_001_m01_034: And so I find myself quite unable to abandon\nthis child.
MID_EV14_001_m01_035: Sir, no! That's Bjor the Recruiter. Nose in on his\nbusiness, and you're like to lose your nose!
MID_EV14_001_m01_036: He's got ties to powerful people, see, and they can\nmake bad things happen.
MID_EV14_001_m01_037: I am obliged to you for the warning. However, I can't\nsay I care.
MID_EV14_001_m01_038: Look at this dumb bastard... What do you think\nyou're doing?
MID_EV14_001_m01_039: What's this?
MID_EV14_002_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_002_m01_001: Well, well, well, lookee what we have here! It's the\ndancer everyone's been goin' on about.
MID_EV14_002_m01_002: You're even finer than I imagined. You could pull in\na pretty penny, that's for sure.
MID_EV14_002_m01_003: How about you come with me. I'll buy you anything\nyou want.
MID_EV14_002_m01_004: Ooh, anything? I like the sound of that! Do tell\nme more.
MID_EV14_002_m01_005: Quick to answer—Bjor likes that. And don't you\nworry. I'll tell you allll about my plans.
MID_EV14_002_m01_006: But right now, I'm gonna reserve this tavern for my\nown private show!
MID_EV14_002_m01_007: Anyone not on my invite list had better get out,\nand fast!
MID_EV14_002_m01_008: Hehehe...
MID_EV14_002_m01_009: You sure do have a lot of money...for a man who was\nthrown out of the viceroy's office for fraud.
MID_EV14_002_m01_010: Who knew recruiting could be so profitable. Or do\nyou just have a generous patron?
MID_EV14_002_m01_011: What?! What have you heard? And who the hell are\nyou, anyway?
MID_EV14_002_m01_012: Bjor the Recruiter is what they call you, but your\nreal name is Bjor Flein.
MID_EV14_002_m01_013: You were so naughty when you served the viceroy's\noffice...embezzling, selling goods on the black market.
MID_EV14_002_m01_014: You got caught and kicked out, but you went on\nusing your connections to do some very bad things.
MID_EV14_002_m01_015: But what really matters to me is that you're one of\nthe scumbags behind the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_002_m01_016: For that, I'd like you to apologize to my father.\nYou'll be meeting him shortly...on the other side.
MID_EV14_002_m01_017: I heard rumors that some woman was killing my old\nfriends one by one.
MID_EV14_002_m01_018: I've been keeping an eye out for you. Never\nthought you'd show up in a place like this.
MID_EV14_002_m01_019: Oh, hey...it's allll coming together now. Your father...\nThat means you're... But c'mon, there's no way.
MID_EV14_002_m01_020: Hehe. Look, I appreciate you coming to me.\nMakes things easier, doesn't it?
MID_EV14_002_m01_021: Oh my! You need all these guards to protect\nyou from one little girl?
MID_EV14_002_m01_022: Go on—yap all ya like. Survival is all that matters,\nas far as I'm concerned.
MID_EV14_002_m01_023: Oh, and mark my words, little girl—I'm going to hurt\nyou until you name the person who ratted me out.
MID_EV14_002_m01_024: I'll take care of these puny guards, milady.\nYou focus on Bjor.
MID_EV14_002_m01_025: You've gotta be joking! You're still alive too?!
MID_EV14_002_m01_026: I don't know what this is all about, but I'm in no\nmood to ignore it. So, I think I shall assist you.
MID_EV14_002_m01_027: I suspect it's about to get considerably violent in\nhere. It would be best if you stay back.
MID_EV14_002_m01_028: You're so stupid! You better keep your hands off me,\nyou creep!
MID_EV14_002_m01_029: You're all stupid! And it's time I show you what I do\nto people dumb enough to cross me.
MID_EV14_003_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_003_m01_001: Stop, please—enough. It's not me you want.\nI'm nobody.
MID_EV14_003_m01_002: I was just following Balboa's orders. Please, let me go.
MID_EV14_003_m01_003: Then tell me, oh magnificent Bjor—where can\nI find Balboa and Lechner?
MID_EV14_003_m01_004: I don't know where Lechner is. I never knew much\nabout him, and I'd like to keep it that way.
MID_EV14_003_m01_005: But I do know where you can find Balboa! She's been\nin Kassite ever since...the siege.
MID_EV14_003_m01_006: Of course, that shrew is the viceroy of Cydonia\nnow. It won't be easy to get to her.
MID_EV14_003_m01_007: Just tell me where my mother is, Bjor!
MID_EV14_003_m01_008: You talked to her near Mahón Castle six months ago!\nI know you did!
MID_EV14_003_m01_009: Where did you take her?!
MID_EV14_003_m01_010: Back then, I sent everyone I recruited to Balboa.
MID_EV14_003_m01_011: I don't know exactly what she's doing, but she's been\nrounding up a lot of cheap labor.
MID_EV14_003_m01_012: My bet is she put them all to work in the mines.
MID_EV14_003_m01_013: What mines? I don't remember any mines\nnear Kassite.
MID_EV14_003_m01_014: Are you lying?! If I go to Kassite, she had better\nbe there!
MID_EV14_003_m01_015: Look, are we done here? I ratted out Balboa, so I get\nto go free, right?
MID_EV14_003_m01_016: I don't suppose killing you will bring my father back...
MID_EV14_003_m01_017: Yeah, exactly. Can't do a thing about that now.
MID_EV14_003_m01_018: Then again, I am very, very angry...and I can't do a\nthing about that either. So, do apologize to my father.
MID_EV14_003_m01_019: Urrgrgluh...
MID_EV14_003_m01_020: Ugh.
MID_EV14_003_m01_021: He's— He's dead? Really? Dead?!
MID_EV14_003_m01_022: That was too much for the poor kid. Hey, are you\nalright? Take a deep breath.
MID_EV14_003_m01_023: I-I'm sorry. I've never watched anyone die before.\nH-he died...right in front of me.
MID_EV14_003_m01_024: Yes, he did. And you don't have to pretend to be\nOK with it.
MID_EV14_003_m01_025: A child should never have to see that kind of thing.\nThis business isn't for you.
MID_EV14_003_m01_026: That takes care of Bjor. Only two more now.
MID_EV14_003_m01_027: I can't wait to meet you, General Balboa.
MID_EV14_003_m01_028: You will scream as you die, and that sound will be\nthe most beautiful song to my ears.
MID_EV14_003_m01_029: That list... She's crossing off the names of the people\nshe's killed...with their own blood.
MID_EV14_003_m01_030: You've found yourself wrapped up in milady's\nvendetta. I'm sorry.
MID_EV14_003_m01_031: Wait, please! You're going to Kassite, aren't you?
MID_EV14_003_m01_032: Take me with you! I can be useful, I swear.
MID_EV14_003_m01_033: You look very pale. Are you sure you're alright?
MID_EV14_003_m01_034: Traveling with this woman is almost certain to bring\nmore shock and heartache. You must know that.
MID_EV14_003_m01_035: Please! I promise I won't hold you back! Give me\na chance.
MID_EV14_003_m01_036: Milady... I don't know about this.
MID_EV14_003_m01_037: You can do whatever you want. But I'm not looking\nout for you.
MID_EV14_003_m01_038: In that case, I think I will accompany you as well.
MID_EV14_003_m01_039: I am like the wind. Quiet. Free. You're welcome to\npay me no mind. It won't hurt my feelings.
MID_EV14_003_m01_040: Well now, I really must take more side trips. One\nstumbles upon the most unexpected things!
MID_EV14_003_m01_041: That girl is finally making her move. I wonder how\nrevenge tastes on her tongue.
MID_EV14_003_m01_042: Sweet like honey? Or bitter like coffee?
MID_EV14_003_m01_043: Hahaha. Guillermo's daughter... Yes, things are\nfinally starting to get interesting.